    "created_at": "2018-08-15T21:04:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-15T21:05:45Z",
    "body": "> `fieldset > legend` wouldn't have the padding if there's a `display: contents` between\r\n\r\nI am a little surprised that this even works (successfully generates a legend in the top border of the fieldset), but apparently it does produce a legend (as tested in Firefox/Chrome). My testcase is here: https://jsfiddle.net/xmcpsozh/\r\n\r\nAnd indeed, Firefox has 0px of padding on the legend inside of `display:contents` there, which does seem a bit arbitrary.  Given this and the other engines' consensus on this, it seems reasonable to change Firefox to match.",
